        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3e020efa-f222-517c-b082-acf2de311b8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: .45 G.A.P., .45 ACP\n- People: Ernest Durham, Gaston Glock\n- Companies: CCI/Speer, Glock Ges.m.b.H.\n- Places: Deutsch-Wagram, Austria\n- Topics: pistol cartridges, firearms manufacturing\n\nFacts:\n- Ernest Durham, an engineer with CCI/Speer, designed the .45 G.A.P. pistol cartridge at Glock’s request.\n- The .45 G.A.P. cartridge was designed to match the power of the .45 ACP, use a stronger case head to reduce case neck blowouts, and be shorter so it could fit in a more compact handgun.\n- Glock Ges.m.b.H., trademarked as GLOCK, is a weapons manufacturer headquartered in Deutsch-Wagram, Austria.\n- Glock Ges.m.b.H. was named after its founder, Gaston Glock.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7054c117-7167-5cd6-b86c-30fb876ed1bd",
        "text": "Page: .45 GAP. Sentence: The .45 G.A.P. (often called the .45 \"GAP\") pistol cartridge was designed by Ernest Durham, an engineer with CCI/Speer, at the request of firearms manufacturer Glock to provide a cartridge that would equal the power of the .45 ACP, have a stronger case head to reduce the possibility of case neck blowouts, and shorter to fit in a more compact handgun.\nPage: Glock Ges.m.b.H.. Sentence: (trademarked as GLOCK) is a weapons manufacturer headquartered in Deutsch-Wagram, Austria, named after its founder, Gaston Glock.",
